---
import ModuleWrapper, { type _ModuleWrapper, type _ModuleHeader } from "@/components/ui/modules/ModuleWrapper.astro";

export interface Props extends _ModuleWrapper {}

const props = Astro.props;

const header: _ModuleHeader = {
	...props.header,
	title: props.header?.title || "Learning and problem-solving",
};
---

<ModuleWrapper {...{ ...props, header }}>
	<div class="space-y-4">
		<div class="space-y-4">
			<p>
				Every project at the agency started the same way. A business I knew nothing about, an owner who knew it completely, and a proposal due. Around 160 of those across about 40 clients:
				e-commerce, membership platforms, learning systems, trades.
			</p>
			<p>
				Almost all of those customers were non-technical. They were not hiring me because I knew their industry, and they were not really hiring me for the code either. They came to me because
				I made the process simple enough to follow. Being the person who could take someone through something they did not understand is what I actually got paid for.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
			<h3 class="text-lg">Where the curiosity comes from</h3>
			<p>
				I wanted to understand how people thought and behaved, so I became a coach. I found myself running a business for the first time, so I learnt sales, customer service and leadership. I
				got curious about how websites work, and that is when I started programming.
			</p>
			<p>
				<span class="text-bad">It can be draining.</span> I am always pushing to the next level, looking for the next thing to apply myself to. It makes me effective and it can get chaotic.
			</p>
			<p><strong>If I don't know how to do something, I can learn how.</strong> Everything I can do, I learnt because the work in front of me needed it that week.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</ModuleWrapper>
